From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:18:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ==== damos core filter fixup ====

mm/damon: treat DAMOS core filters as a primary target selection method

DAMOS access pattern and core filters are treated as a primary and a
secondary target selection method, respectively.  DAMOS target regions
are initially selected with the access pattern, and later evaluated for
the core filters only when needed, in the middle of lower level
operations.  DAMOS qutoa goal type eligible_mem_bp is ignoring the core
filters.

There is no real reason to treat DAMOS core filters as a secondary
method, though.  DAMOS stats treat core filter rejections same to access
pattern-based rejections.  The core filters are effectively applied for
every operations.  The duplicated handling of the filters in each
operation only make it easy to make mistakes.

Promote DAMOS core filters to a primary target selection method.  Use it
in the central high level place that DAMOS access pattern is handled.
One consequence of this change is the behavioral change of
eligible_mem_bp DAMOS quota goal type.  It was ignoring core filters.
Now it aware of it.  It is difficult to imagine real users that depend
on the old behavior.  And the new behavior is more intuitive in my
opinion.

Remove unit tests that were too duplicated and will fail after the
change, via patch 1.  Make the promotion via patch 2.  Clarify the
changed eligible_mem_bp behavior on the design document, via patch 3.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
